    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Type 2 diabetes mellitus with peripheral artery disease: cramping in both calves after about one and a half blocks of walking, worse on the right, easing within minutes of rest; no rest pain, wounds, or color change. Resting ankle-brachial index 0.62 right and 0.74 left, toe-brachial index 0.46 and 0.55; dorsalis pedis and posterior tibial pulses absent on the right and faint on the left. A1c 8.6% on metformin, glipizide and glargine, with low glucose readings (to 52 mg/dL) after late performances. Foot: protective sensation intact to the 10-g monofilament at all sites and to vibration; callus under the second metatarsal heads; hammer toes of the second and third toes; no ulcer (IWGDF risk category 2). Synthetic modern episode linked to her documented diabetes and its circulatory complications</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E11.51</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the type of diabetes was not made public and is synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Moderate nonproliferative diabetic retinopathy with center-involving diabetic macular edema in the right eye (best-corrected acuity 64 letters, about 20/50) and moderate nonproliferative retinopathy without macular edema in the left eye (81 letters); lens implants in both eyes from earlier cataract surgery. Synthetic modern episode linked to her documented diabetic eye problems</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E11.3311</td><td>S — Synthetic modern eye diagnosis on retinal imaging and optical coherence tomography in the clinic; the left eye is described in the display.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Coronary artery disease after five-vessel coronary bypass surgery last year, with an intensive care stay; no angina now; on aspirin, a statin, and metoprolol. Synthetic modern episode linked to her documented heart surgery</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I25.10</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of her documented heart surgery; bypass grafts are described in the display.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

